Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

• orders.id / orders.customer_id / orders.ordered  
  – identify the sales‑order we are analysing (order 421).  

• picking_line.order_id / picking_line.product_id / picking_line.qty / picking_line.picklist_id / picking_line.line_no  
  – holds every individual “pick” that was executed for a given order.  
  – qty will be averaged per product.  
  – line_no gives the physical FIFO sequence inside each pick‑list.  

• picking_list.id / picking_list.created  
  – ties several picking_line records together; used only to show which pick‑list(s) belong to the order.  

• products.id / products.name  
  – translate product_id to human readable product names.  


Conditions that will be applied  

• picking_line.order_id = 421   (limit to the required order)  
• GROUP BY picking_line.product_id (to calculate the average qty per product)  
• JOIN products   (to fetch the product names)  
• Optional ORDER BY products.name (for nice presentation).  



Below are 10 exploratory SQL queries – from very simple look‑ups to the final answer – each limited to 20 rows.

```sql
-- 1) List the order we are interested in
SELECT *
FROM orders
WHERE id = 421
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Find all pick‑lists that contain lines for order 421
SELECT DISTINCT picklist_id
FROM picking_line
WHERE order_id = 421
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Show every pick‑line belonging to order 421 (FIFO sequence visible by line_no)
SELECT picklist_id,
       line_no,
       product_id,
       qty
FROM picking_line
WHERE order_id = 421
ORDER BY picklist_id,
         line_no
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Translate the product_ids from the previous query into product names
SELECT pl.product_id,
       p.name
FROM picking_line  AS pl
JOIN products      AS p ON p.id = pl.product_id
WHERE pl.order_id = 421
GROUP BY pl.product_id, p.name          -- DISTINCT effect
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Calculate the average quantity picked PER PRODUCT for order 421
SELECT product_id,
       AVG(qty) AS avg_qty
FROM picking_line
WHERE order_id = 421
GROUP BY product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Same as (5) but with product names
SELECT pl.product_id,
       p.name,
       AVG(pl.qty) AS avg_qty
FROM picking_line AS pl
JOIN products     AS p ON p.id = pl.product_id
WHERE pl.order_id = 421
GROUP BY pl.product_id, p.name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Show FIFO details: every individual pick in chronological sequence
SELECT pl.picklist_id,
       pl.line_no,
       pl.product_id,
       p.name,
       pl.qty
FROM picking_line AS pl
JOIN products     AS p ON p.id = pl.product_id
WHERE pl.order_id = 421
ORDER BY pl.picklist_id,
         pl.line_no
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Total quantity picked per product for order 421 (not averaged)
SELECT product_id,
       SUM(qty) AS total_qty
FROM picking_line
WHERE order_id = 421
GROUP BY product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) (Context) Average qty per product across ALL orders
SELECT product_id,
       AVG(qty) AS avg_qty_all_orders
FROM picking_line
GROUP BY product_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER:
--     Which products were picked for order 421 and the average number of
--     units picked for each product (FIFO already obeyed by the pick_line
--     sequencing; the average just summarises those lines)
SELECT pl.product_id            AS "Product_ID",
       p.name                   AS "Product_Name",
       ROUND(AVG(pl.qty), 2)    AS "Average_Units_Picked"
FROM picking_line AS pl
JOIN products     AS p  ON p.id = pl.product_id
WHERE pl.order_id = 421
GROUP BY pl.product_id, p.name
ORDER BY p.name
LIMIT 20;
```

Running the final query will return one row per product that took part in order 421 together with the average number of units (across all its FIFO pick‑lines) that were picked for that product.
